mindmap
  root((Schnorr ZKP\nSecurity Properties))
    Zero-Knowledge
      Password x never transmitted over the network
      Server only receives the public value y = G^x mod P
      Server learns nothing about x from the protocol transcript
      A simulator can reproduce a valid transcript without knowing x
    Soundness
      Cannot forge a valid proof without knowing the private key x
      Security reduces to the Discrete Logarithm Problem
      Safe prime P is 2048-bit — computationally infeasible to factor
      Session challenge c is fresh and unpredictable
    Completeness
      An honest prover with correct x always produces an accepted proof
      Verification identity: G^s = G^(r+cx) = G^r · (G^x)^c = t · y^c (mod P)
    Forward Secrecy
      Random r is generated fresh per login session via CSPRNG
      Compromise of a JWT token does not reveal the password
      Historical sessions cannot be decrypted from a leaked token
    Replay Attack Prevention
      Server challenge c is random and single-use
      Duplicate commitment for same client_id is rejected with 409
      In-memory session state is cleared after verify
    Credential Security
      KDF: SHA-256 applied to username:password before mod Q
      Server stores only the public key y, never the password
      Brute-force is bounded by group order Q (2047-bit)
    Transport and API Security
      CORS enforced on all routes
      X-Frame-Options DENY — clickjacking prevention
      Content-Security-Policy default-src self
      HSTS header applied on secure connections
      X-Content-Type-Options nosniff
      Request-ID tracing on every request and response
    Data Minimisation
      Only client_id and y stored at registration
      Personal data access requires a valid JWT
      Full account deletion via forgetme cascades all records
